The peregrine falcon holds the title for the fastest animal in the world when it comes to diving speeds. It can reach up to 240 miles per hour (386 kilometers per hour) during its hunting dive, also known as stooping. This makes it the quickest creature on Earth.

However, if we consider horizontal speed over a distance, the cheetah is the fastest land animal, capable of reaching speeds up to about 70 miles per hour (112 kilometers per hour).